Based on the code snippets and the failing test related to XPath `following::node()`, the issue seems to be specifically in the `DOMNodePointer` class implementation where the `node()` method incorrectly checks for only `ELEMENT_NODE` and `DOCUMENT_NODE` types instead of allowing any node type. The fix should involve updating this logic to allow any node type when processing the `node()` function.

